    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Australia made a new rule in December 2025. The government said children under 16 cannot use "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "social media",
            "zh": "社交媒体"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The goal was to keep kids safe online."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But a new study shows the rule is not working very well. Researchers asked about 1,000 children aged 12 to 15. Many of them said they still can use their social media "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "accounts",
            "zh": "账号"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". About 61% of the children were still able to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "log in",
            "zh": "登录"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some children said the rule does not change their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "safety",
            "ref": "v-safety"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They think it has little "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "effect",
            "zh": "影响"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on them. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "law",
            "ref": "v-law"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " does not "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "punish",
            "ref": "v-punish"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " children or parents. It asks social media companies to follow the rules. If companies do not follow them, they may need to pay a large "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "fine",
            "zh": "罚款"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some people compare this rule with China’s online game limits for "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "teenagers",
            "zh": "青少年"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". In China, children under 18 can usually play online games only for a short time on weekends and holidays. The rule "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "aims",
            "ref": "v-aim"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to protect young people’s health and study time. However, some teenagers still find ways to play longer. This shows that it can be difficult to fully control young people’s online activities."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Other countries are now watching Australia’s social media ban closely. They want to know if it really helps children. People are still "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "discussing",
            "ref": "v-discuss"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " if social media bans are useful for young students."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
